  "material_audit": [
    "Printed steps specify black concrete, stone bricks and stone-brick stairs; note mentions mossy stone bricks. Foundation black area7x7 is surrounded by dark terrace surface inferred from subsequent images.",
    "Printed walls: mangrove planks, stairs and fences; white wool; glass panes. Stair entry is open: no invented doors or hinges.",
    "Printed eaves: oxidized cut copper slabs and stairs; text says copper may be waxed with honeycomb. Waxed oxidized variants preserve the illustrated final colour.",
    "Printed finial: gold blocks, anvils and iron bars. Selected one gold block, three vertically stacked north-facing anvils, one unconnected iron-bar tip from enlarged diagram.",
    "Interiors shown for rooms1 and2: mangrove stair/slab tables, barrels, lanterns, dark foliage/potted plants, cyan seat/carpet accents. Plant species and exact locations are inferred; barrels have no inventory NBT."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Exactly one distinct building. Steps1..9 are sequential stages; Room1 and Room2 are furnishing cutaways of this pagoda, not separate standalone buildings.",
    "All ordered images were read visually. Printed dimensions override perspective. There is no printed overall height or upper room measurement; all upper proportions, y-levels and concealed geometry are inferred, not exact recovery.",
    "Five wall shells use9x9,9x9,9x9,7x7,5x5 outside widths and4 wall courses each. Main render shows a blank front panel on the third room, paired windows on fourth, one on fifth. Other window locations are symmetry-based inferences.",
    "15x15 two-course stone podium has a7x7 black centre within the ground room and black terrace walking surface. No extra landscape, trees, players, clouds, terrain or detached scenery.",
    "Balcony at y6 is15x15 mangrove planks with perimeter fences aty7 and two-high corner posts; ground-to-balcony corner fence struts are aty3..5. Topological supports are inferred.",
    "Ground interior four-step north-facing mangrove staircase atx4,z7..4 connects ground floor to balcony through deliberately open landing cells. All higher floors use continuous west-facing ladders x8,z7,y7..28 backed by mangrove planksx9; the backing inside wider rooms is an inferred support column.",
    "Copper eaves use stair rims, inner bottom-slab edges, timber central flooring, 2x2 diagonal corner extensions and bottom slabs on the far tips. Exact half-height and corner block distribution cannot be uniquely read. Four hanging lanterns occur under each copper-eave corner.",
    "Final copper roof has four shrinking square courses plus a top-slab cap. A gold block rests directly on that cap; finial y positions and anvil count are visual estimates.",
    "Ground and second rooms include only the two displayed furnishing arrangements; upper room furniture is not shown and remains empty. Potted oak saplings and persistent oak leaves stand in for visually ambiguous potted greenery; no complex block-entity NBT or inventories.",
    "Fence/pane connections match immediate encoded full-block and same-kind neighbors; stairs explicitly encode facing,half,shape; slabs encode bottom/top; ladders face west toward their west-side exposed face and east backing. No door exists in the reference entry so no door state is invented.",
    "No entities, fluids, complex NBT, signs or live-server tests. Registry and full-state reader failures must be reported without changing intended states to conceal them.",
    "Local validation proves artifact consistency and registry legality, not exact photographic recovery, gravity/neighbor-update stability, placement order, pathfinding or live-server success."
  ],
